{"claim_id": "CT-S9-PVPARAMS-C014", "task_id": "CT-S9-PVPARAMS", "claim": "The scalar local data alone do not exhibit a Jimbo Lax embedding or a PV deformation time for System C.", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "REPORT.md structural analysis", "output_hash": "B515657108E8B4C62EA362C8B1E0EED98B766718438790E882517155C10A6BFF", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "review": "self", "audit_r5": "Backfilled per ruling 1. Audited in CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S9.md and SHARPENED there: the PV time is not merely unexhibited, it is FIXED at t = -/+ 2i*sqrt(33)/9 by Jimbos normalisation of the irregular part at infinity. Stays review=self: the audit had full access to the derivation history and so was not a cold read.", "review_note": "self: checked only by the session that produced it. For a computation this means no independent reimplementation; re-running the original script would not change this."}
